/haseuleriantrail","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether some trail uses every edge exactly once: the graph is Eulerian, or exactly one vertex has out − in = 1, one has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in − out = 1, the rest are balanced, and the vertices with edges are weakly connected."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"True for every edgeless graph."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/hasEulerianTrail","title":"hasEulerianTrail","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"hasEulerianTrail"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}]},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/shortestTour(weight:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest directed tour (the asymmetric travelling salesman problem), by the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Held–Karp program as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph.shortestTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":": the least-weight Hamiltonian cycle of the simple digraph, each step along an arc"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from one vertex to the next, or nil when there is none; among the optimal ones, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first vertex. Self-loops are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored and each ordered pair is joined by its lightest arc (the earliest position on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ties), which is the edge the returned "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cycle"},{"type":"text","text":" uses, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cycle.weight(weight)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the tour’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length. "},{"type":"codeVoice"